## Modern Language Obsolescence

Many GOF patterns were designed for Java and C++. Modern languages provide built-in
mechanisms that make the manual pattern scaffolding unnecessary.

**Always prefer the language-native mechanism first.**

### Patterns Largely Obsolete or Simplified

| Pattern | Modern Replacement | Languages |
|---|---|---|
| Singleton | Language-level singletons, dependency injection, top-level functions | Rust, Go, Swift, Kotlin, Python, JS |
| Factory Method | Generics, constructors with default params, dependency injection | C#, Rust, TypeScript, Kotlin |
| Abstract Factory | Generics, builder patterns, DI containers | Most modern languages |
| Builder | Named parameters, records, data classes, builder libraries | Kotlin, Python, Rust, TypeScript, Java 21+ |
| Prototype | Built-in cloning, copy-with-modifiers, immutable data types | Python, Rust, Swift, Kotlin |
| Strategy | Closures, lambdas, first-class functions | All modern languages |
| Command | Closures, lambdas, function objects | All modern languages |
| Template Method | Closures, higher-order functions, composition | All modern languages |
| Observer | Reactive streams, event emitters, async iterators, signals | Swift, Kotlin, JS, Rust, C#, Python |
| Iterator | Language iteration protocols, range-based for, forEach | All modern languages |
| Visitor | Pattern matching, algebraic data types, sealed types | Rust, Swift, Kotlin, TypeScript, F# |
| State | Algebraic data types, sealed classes with pattern matching | Rust, Swift, Kotlin, TypeScript |
| Chain of Responsibility | Middleware pipelines, interceptor chains, async streams | Express, Rails middleware, ASP.NET, Rust |
| Memento | Immutable value types, snapshots, versioned state | Rust, Swift, Kotlin, Elm |

### Patterns Still Useful (with adaptations)

| Pattern | Modern Form | When Still Needed |
|---|---|---|
| Adapter | Wrapper functions, translation layers, protocol extensions | Integrating incompatible APIs |
| Decorator | Middleware, higher-order components, extension functions | Cross-cutting behavior (logging, caching, auth) |
| Facade | Simplified module exports, convenience APIs | Exposing coherent sub-system interfaces |
| Proxy | Lazy evaluation, memoization decorators, virtual proxies | Access control, lazy loading, caching |
| Composite | Recursive data structures, tree types | Hierarchical component systems |
| Flyweight | Interning, object pools, string interning | Large numbers of identical objects |
| Mediator | Event buses, pub/sub, message brokers | Complex object coordination |
| Specification | Composable predicates, query builders | Business rule composition |
| Null Object | Option/Result types, sealed unions | Safe absence handling |

